 state←ReadStormFile filename;lines;fields;records
⍝ Reads the storm guard's file and returns its contents; see `NewStormState`.\\
⍝ A file that does not exist yields an empty state; one that cannot be parsed signals an error.
 state←NewStormState
 :If ⎕NEXISTS filename
     lines←⊃⎕NGET filename 1
     lines←(0<≢¨lines)/lines
     lines←('#'≠⊃¨lines)/lines                  ⍝ Comments
     fields←{⍵⊆⍨⍵≠⎕UCS 9}¨lines
     records←('signature'∘≡¨⊃¨fields)/fields
     :If 0<≢records
         'Invalid signature record'⎕SIGNAL 11/⍨∨/7≠≢¨records
         state.signatures←2⊃¨records
         state.counts←ToNumber¨3⊃¨records
         state.lastFulls←ToNumber¨4⊃¨records
         state.firsts←IsoToSeconds¨5⊃¨records
         state.lasts←IsoToSeconds¨6⊃¨records
         state.lastFullTimes←IsoToSeconds¨7⊃¨records
     :EndIf
     records←('full'∘≡¨⊃¨fields)/fields
     :If 0<≢records
         'Invalid full-treatment record'⎕SIGNAL 11/⍨∨/2≠≢¨records
         state.fulls←IsoToSeconds¨2⊃¨records
     :EndIf
 :EndIf
